    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0511" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6176 F 51/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harvey S.
                            Firestone to Mr. W. D.
                        Hines</hi><anchor n="33" xml:id="d356-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Akron, Ohio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Desire you remain. Cable outline proposed changes leaving agreements intact. Mail
                    full confirmations promptly. Changes ninety nine to fifty years with renewal
                    made request Secretary Hughes more fair Liberia, I consented.</p>
                <p>Impossible make loan unless Liberian finances are administered by parties making
                    loan. Liberia fortunate having our Government take responsibility helping
                    administer loan. If they could understand our <pb facs="0512" n="430"
                        xml:id="pg430"/> Government and my desire have agreements fair and workable
                    there could be no objections agreements as submitted. We have no thought or
                    desire of depriving them of their independence. I trust no suggestion is made
                    that will disturb confidence.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>British Restriction Act irritating Americans. Rubber today 60 cents. Reported
                    British rubber manufacturers appear in Parliament tomorrow petitioning
                    rescinding of restriction act. This sure come sooner or later. We will lose our
                    opportunity for raising large capital.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey S.
                    Firestone</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d356-f1" n="33" type="source" xml:id="d356-f1-content">
